    "turn_idx": 288,
    "turn_text": "And if we can get on that track, I think we could put a coalition together, which became like Roosevelt did this. It was poor farmers and poor immigrants and women. And it was all of these groups that became a coalition that lasted from the Great Depression until 1980. And we grew the largest middle class. Civil rights got done. We went to the moon, Tennessee Valley. Talk about growth, right? Interstate highway. Yeah, I mean, the science, technology, the internet. I mean, all of these things like sprung out of that idea. And then it got torn down. And now I think we're ready to rebuild. So can you imagine a world where we're talking about social emotional learning in every school. What we feed our kids in our schools is healthy food that keeps them from getting diabetes at the rates that we're getting them now. You know, a prison system where you're teaching these kind of techniques to people so that they don't go out of prison and come back in. Taking care of our teachers and our healthcare workers, our doctors, that can actually teach mindfulness-based stress reduction",
